Five Below's table shows 157 stores opened and 7 closed in fiscal 2025, for a net increase of 150 and 1,921 stores at year end [1]. For comparison, 228 stores were opened in fiscal 2024 (227 net) [1], and 205 in fiscal 2023 (204 net) [1].

For growth, the company plans to open approximately 150 net new stores in fiscal 2026, through expansion in existing markets and by entering new markets [2]. It had executed lease agreements for 73 new stores in fiscal 2026 as of January 31, 2026 [3]. Over the longer term, it believes it has the opportunity to grow its store base to more than 3,500 locations [4], up from the current 1,921 locations across 46 states.

Most near-term growth is expected to come from store densification in existing markets, as well as new markets [3]. When entering new markets, the company opens multiple stores in a single market on the same day (clustering) [5]. Its new store model assumes about 9,500 square feet, roughly $2 million in first-year sales, and an average cash investment of about $0.4 million, with a targeted payback of about one year [5].

The filing cautions that the actual number, location and timing of 2026 openings will depend on factors such as retail trends, competition, the economic environment, and the ability to hire and retain store managers and crew [2].